  "id": "analytic-third",
  "term": "analytic third",
  "definition": "In psychoanalytic thinking, the analytic third is an unlocalized shared subjectivity that emerges within the patient-analyst relationship. It refers to an unconscious, intersubjective meaning-making process, expressed through the analytic couple’s patterns of interaction, that helps generate new ways of relating and understanding the self.",
